<title>BRAZIL: Bankruptcy, debt relief filings down in Sao Paulo.</title>
<headline>Bankruptcy, debt relief filings down in Sao Paulo.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Filings for debt relief and bankruptcies in Sao Paulo fell 17 percent and 22 percent, respectively, in January compared with the same month 1996, the Centralized Bank Services (Serasa) said in a statement.</p>
<p>Bankruptcy filings reached 773 and debt relief requests hit 24 in January, the statement said.</p>
<p>Serasa said January debt relief filings rose 26 percent against December, when 19 firms filed for debt relief and filings for bankruptcy last month dropped 21 percent against December.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
